              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MISSMIKE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I used Dole - Orange Pineapple Banana juice and it was perfect. I will be making these again!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chazsabo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! To save time, Skip the blender and ice and just throw these into a freezer-safe pitcher and freeze overnight. I make a similar bahama mama recipe for parties and freeze a huge cooler full of them. No blending, no ice and they come out perfect every time! Depending on the size of the batch I make, I always check on them in the morning to see if they need time to thaw a little, but it saves alot of time and aggrevation of dealing with a blender! I also add a bag of Dole frozen fruit(peaches/mango/pineapple) to them!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-21T10:20:03.473Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PrincessAnna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a party just mixed a large batch in a pitcher, stirred and put in the fridge to chill. Used Blue Chair Bay Coconut and white rum. Served over ice instead of mixing in blender - this was just easier for a large group. Everyone loved it the drink was a big hit!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-22T03:23:00.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I don’t add the ice so when I make it it’s not a frozen drink. I serve it over ice so it turns out to be a little stronger and then I throw in a dark rum floater right before serving. Everybody loves these!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-31T22:13:03.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nuggets"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is SO good!!! I put 3 ice cubes in a shaker with the other ingredients and shook it up and served it over the ice instead of blending it together. I did double the recipe and I would call that one serving. It is also great with Dole's Orange Peach &amp; Mango juice in place of the o.j. and pineapple juice. YUM!",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-30T07:33:26.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! Unfortunately I didn't have any coconut rum, so I just doubled the spiced rum and I thought it still had great flavor. I don't love slushy bahama mama's, so I just mixed it together in my cocktail shaker and then poured it over ice. I would definitely make this again! Excited to try it again with the coconut rum and the orange pineapple banana juice that some reviewers mentioned.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-28T21:28:05.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SavvyBroth1762"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is actually a really solid recipe used by pros. It’s been 12 years, might as well reveal that Chazsabo’s trick to freeze the entire solution into a sorbet-like state and serve individually has since been utilized by several world-class cocktail bars to make thousands of these at one time and then serve them already pre-prepared to guests. They are simply ordered, removed from the cooler and agitated briefly with a bartender’s mixing spoon, then served for the same price as a legitimate mixed cocktail",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-25T03:45:12.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "yogimiss"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this last night. Love Bahama Mama's however, this one was too weak. If you make it a slush, it weakens the taste, imo. I think it's best shaken not slushed. I'll try it over ice next time around to see if this theory hold outs. Overall, nice flavor...just weak. I also added half the grenadine that the recipe called for.",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-02T12:37:34.117Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shaz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful flavor. We added just a splash of amaretto liquer (just a splash, it's strong and too much will permeate the drink) to perfect this recipe. We didn't \"slush\" it (I only like that in daquaris), but rather, poured everything over a generous glass of crushed ice. Add the grenadine first and the alcohol last, and the color of the drink will look like a fading sunset. This is the perfect summer drink for relaxing after work or on weekends.",
            "datePublished": "2007-06-12T04:59:49.793Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rosey Richards"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is pretty close to how you are suppose to make a Bahama Mama , But you are suppose to use 1 part light rum, 1 part coconut rum, 1/2 part grenadine, 2 parts orange juice , 2 parts pineapple juice and blend in a blender. You can pour over ice or add ice if you want a slushy type drink. This how they make it in the Bahamas. Substitute the word part with oz , cup ,pint or whatever.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-31T02:43:34.047Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Connie-O"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great reviews from my Memorial Day gang. I made them by the pitcher so guests could easily serve themselves over cubed ice. I reduced the amount of grenadine by half because the \"test\" drinks were way too sweet. Also used Dole orange/pineapple juice. I always have a signature cocktail for Memorial Day and this is the best so far.",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-06T09:06:34.373Z"
          },
          {
